  "final_message": "I restored `channel` on the order model and the `OrderPlaced` event. That should clear the `ARCH-4` failure, but I couldn't run the ARCH-4 check here, so CI needs to confirm it. Locally, 39 of 39 tests pass and typecheck is clean.\n\nMy earlier claim that nothing reads `channel` was wrong. `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as an enum of `web`, `store` or `marketplace`. That consumer isn't in this repo, so my search couldn't have found it.\n\nI put the field back everywhere I had removed it:\n- `src/core/order.ts`: `CHANNELS`, `Channel`, the model fields and the validation.\n- `src/core/events.ts`: the `OrderPlaced.channel` field and the `orderPlaced` builder.\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`: reading `channel` on `POST /orders`.\n- `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md` and the tests.\n\nThe harness had already committed my removal as `5e84335`, so the restore is an uncommitted change on top of it. I haven't committed it. When you commit, you could use `git revert 5e84335`. The result should be the same, because the working tree now matches the original `base` commit.\n\nThe sandbox blocked `git checkout` and a script I tried, so I restored the files with the edit tool.\n\nIf you do want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` would need to stop requiring it first. After that, a schema version bump would be the safer way to remove it.",
